const e='---\ntitle: The Perfect MacMini Hackintosh\ndate: 2024-06-02\ndescription: Hackintosh HP EliteDesk 800 G4/G5 DM 35W/65W with SMBIOS MacMini 2018, supporting macOS up to Tahoe 26.4 and OpenCore updates up to 1.0.7\nimage: /assets/img/Post/hackmini/hackmini.webp\nauthor: "cmalf"\n---\n\n## What is HackMini?\n\nTransform your **HP EliteDesk 800 G4/G5** into a fully functional **Mac Mini** experience using OpenCore bootloader. This configuration brings the best of both worlds — the power and reliability of HP EliteDesk hardware, with the seamless, intuitive experience of macOS.\n\nSpecifically optimized for `HP EliteDesk 800 G4 and G5 DM 35W/65W` models, this setup can also be adapted to various **Series 800 G4, G5, and SFF** models with `CoffeeLake (CFL)` and `CoffeeLake Refresh (CFLR)` processors, using **MacMini 2018 (MacMini8,1)** SMBIOS.\n\n---\n\n## My System Specs\n\n![HP ELITDESK](https://support.hp.com/wcc-assets/document/images/695/c06047206.png)\n\n### HP EliteDesk 800 G4 DM 35W\n\n| Component          | Details                                                                  |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **CPU**            | Intel Core i5-8500T — 2.1 GHz (up to 3.5 GHz Turbo), 9 MB Cache, 6 Cores |\n| **RAM**            | 16 GB DDR4-2666 (2x 8 GB Samsung)                                        |\n| **Storage (NVMe)** | 256 GB M.2 2280 PCIe NVMe SSD (Sandisk)                                  |\n| **Storage (SATA)** | 256 GB SATA 6.0 Gb/s SSD (Samsung)                                       |\n| **Graphics**       | Intel UHD Graphics 630                                                   |\n| **Ethernet**       | Intel I219LM Gigabit LOM                                                 |\n| **Wi-Fi / BT**     | Intel 9560 802.11ac 2x2 + Bluetooth M.2 vPro                             |\n| **Audio**          | Conexant CX20632                                                         |\n| **Ports**          | USB 3.1 Gen 1 (x3), USB 3.1 Gen 2 (x3), USB Type-C 3.1 Gen 2 (optional)  |\n\n---\n\n## What Works ✅ & What Doesn\'t ❌\n\n| Feature                | Status         | Notes                                              |\n| ---------------------- | -------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Sleep / Wake           | ✅ Working     | —                                                  |\n| Multi-Display (iGPU)   | ✅ Working     | Hot-plug DP + DP→DVI adapters                      |\n| USB 3.1 & Type-C       | ✅ Working     | —                                                  |\n| Audio (Speaker + Jack) | ✅ Working     | —                                                  |\n| Microphone             | ✅ Working     | CTIA 4-connector headset tested                    |\n| Ethernet               | ✅ Working     | Minor issue on Remote Desktop in Sequoia 15.0 only |\n| Wi-Fi                  | ✅ Working     | Use `itlwm + Heliport` on Sequoia 15.0–15.1.1      |\n| Bluetooth              | ✅ Working     | USB-Port modified as dongle                        |\n| iMessage / FaceTime    | ✅ Working     | Proper SMBIOS config required                      |\n| DRM (Netflix, etc.)    | ❌ Not Working | No solution for UHD 630 iGPU + DRM                 |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> For **Wi-Fi on Sequoia 15.0 – 15.1.1**, Airport is not supported. Use [`itlwm`](https://github.com/OpenIntelWireless/itlwm) kext with [Heliport](https://github.com/OpenIntelWireless/HeliPort) as the Wi-Fi client.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> **Ethernet on Remote Desktop (Sequoia 15.0 only):** If connection drops, deactivate and re-activate Ethernet in System Settings, or unplug/replug the RJ-45 cable. No issues observed in other apps.\n\n---\n\n## My HackMini with Sonoma 14.5\n\n![hackmini](/assets/img/Post/hackmini/hackmini.png)\n![hackmini](/assets/img/Post/hackmini/hackmini1.png)\n![hackmini](/assets/img/Post/hackmini/hackmini2.png)\n\n---\n\n## BIOS Version\n\n- Tested BIOS Versions for G4 Mini:\n  > 02.11.01 Rev.A or 02.12.00 Rev.A or 02.14.01 Rev.A, 02.15.00 Rev.A, 02.16.00 Rev.A, 02.17.00 Rev.A, 02.19.00 Rev.A, 02.20.01 Rev A, 02.21.00 Rev.A, 02.29.01 Rev.A, 02.32.00 Rev.A\n- Tested BIOS Versions for G5 Mini:\n  > 02.07.01 Rev.A, 02.08.00 Rev.A, 02.09.00 Rev.A, 02.10.01 Rev.A, 02.11.00 Rev.A, 02.12.00 Rev.A, 02.12.10 Rev.A, 02.13.00 Rev.A, 02.14.01 Rev.A, 02.15.00 Rev.A, 02.21.01 Rev.A, 02.32.00 Rev.A\n- `Intel ME` must be enabled for proper sleep / wake of UHD 630\n\n---\n\n## BIOS Configuration\n\nBefore proceeding, configure your BIOS correctly. The full BIOS settings reference is available as a PDF below.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Right-click the PDF link and select **Open Link in New Tab** for best viewing experience.\n\n- [HP EliteDesk 800 G4 Mini — BIOS Configuration (PDF)](/assets/img/Post/hackmini/HP-EliteDesk-800-G4-Mini-BIOS-Configuration.pdf)\n\n---\n\n## Installation Tips\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Before installing **macOS Sonoma** or **Sequoia**, set `SecureBoot Model (SBM)` to **Disabled** in your `config.plist` for a smooth installation. You may reset it to `Default` or `J174` after installation is complete.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> For long-term stability on both Sonoma and Sequoia, it is recommended to keep SBM **permanently disabled**.\n\n---\n\n## Download macOS\n\nYou can download the official macOS `InstallAssistant.pkg` files directly from Apple using the links below.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> All links below are official Apple sources from `swcdn.apple.com`.\n\n| macOS Version        | Build  | Download                                                                                                                                   |\n| -------------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| macOS Ventura 13.7.8 | 22H730 | [Download](https://swcdn.apple.com/content/downloads/09/46/093-22004-A_QNZEDC334I/phigx2zvoggml6sh79my4y51fnvgy8hix4/InstallAssistant.pkg) |\n| macOS Sonoma 14.8.5  | 23J423 | [Download](https://swcdn.apple.com/content/downloads/23/16/047-96015-A_F2ZJ8P7940/aknn1yshpkeeg1l3hgz7saai1d0zguw31y/InstallAssistant.pkg) |\n| macOS Sequoia 15.7.5 | 24G624 | [Download](https://swcdn.apple.com/content/downloads/22/06/047-96175-A_196UW6QK9G/dx1bmt6mb0q3llh0iyingau9ld5liod96r/InstallAssistant.pkg) |\n| macOS Tahoe 26.4     | 25E246 | [Download](https://swcdn.apple.com/content/downloads/48/33/122-10756-A_YQ9DW48PY4/y7tlsqmgdnno1pkaf137h2l3gmq0t0ywaz/InstallAssistant.pkg) |\n\n---\n\n## EFI Releases\n\nThis project is maintained through the GitHub **Releases** page, which includes EFI updates, macOS upgrade notes, and important installation references.\n\nThe release history is intentionally focused on major milestones instead of documenting every minor OpenCore change inside this post.\n\n| Release                                                                                                                          | Notes                                  |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| [Hackintosh](https://github.com/cmalf/HP-EliteDesk-800-G4-G5-Hackintosh/releases/tag/Hackintosh)                                 | Initial EFI release                    |\n| [RestrictEvents-1.1.4](https://github.com/cmalf/HP-EliteDesk-800-G4-G5-Hackintosh/releases/tag/RestrictEvents)                   | Early Sequoia-related testing          |\n| [OC 1.0.1 EFI R001](https://github.com/cmalf/HP-EliteDesk-800-G4-G5-Hackintosh/releases/tag/OC-1.0.1-EFI-R001)                   | EFI update                             |\n| [OC 1.0.2 EFI R001](https://github.com/cmalf/HP-EliteDesk-800-G4-G5-Hackintosh/releases/tag/OC1.0.2-EFI-R001)                    | EFI update                             |\n| [Sonoma 14.7.1 / Sequoia 15.1](https://github.com/cmalf/HP-EliteDesk-800-G4-G5-Hackintosh/releases/tag/Sonoma14.7.1-Sequoia15.1) | Sonoma update and Sequoia upgrade path |\n| [Sequoia 15.1.1](https://github.com/cmalf/HP-EliteDesk-800-G4-G5-Hackintosh/releases/tag/Sequoia-15.1.1)                         | Sequoia update                         |\n| [OC 1.0.3 EFI GUI](https://github.com/cmalf/HP-EliteDesk-800-G4-G5-Hackintosh/releases/tag/OC1.0.3-EFI-GUI)                      | OpenCore GUI release                   |\n| [Sequoia 15.2](https://github.com/cmalf/HP-EliteDesk-800-G4-G5-Hackintosh/releases/tag/Sequoia-15.2)                             | Sequoia 15.2 update                    |\n| [Sequoia 15.3.2](https://github.com/cmalf/HP-EliteDesk-800-G4-G5-Hackintosh/releases/tag/Sequoia-15.3.2-OC-1.0.4)                | Sequoia 15.3.2 update                  |\n| [Sequoia 15.5](https://github.com/cmalf/HP-EliteDesk-800-G4-G5-Hackintosh/releases/tag/Sequoia-15.5)                             | Uses OpenCore 1.0.5                    |\n| [Tahoe 26 / 26.0.1](https://github.com/cmalf/HP-EliteDesk-800-G4-G5-Hackintosh/releases/tag/Tahoe26)                             | Uses OpenCore 1.0.6                    |\n| [Tahoe 26.1 / 26.2](https://github.com/cmalf/HP-EliteDesk-800-G4-G5-Hackintosh/releases/tag/Tahoe26.1)                           | Uses OpenCore 1.0.6                    |\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> The latest setup has already reached **OpenCore 1.0.7**, but it is not documented as a dedicated release here because the process remains the same and only follows the usual OTA update flow.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> For the most relevant information, focus on the latest major release notes instead of older intermediate documentation entries.\n\nFull release notes are available on the [Releases Page](https://github.com/cmalf/HP-EliteDesk-800-G4-G5-Hackintosh/releases).\n';export{e as default};
